[10.2953, "o", "\r\n"]
[10.3068, "o", "Plan\r\n"]
[10.3216, "o", "  1. Create the administrator account 'homebrew' (UID 600) with your password.\r\n  2. Hide it and set its shell to /usr/bin/false (nobody can log in with it).\r\n  3. Run: chown -R homebrew:admin /opt/homebrew ; chmod -R g-w,o-w /opt/homebrew\r\n  4. Put the brew wrapper in /usr/local/share/homebrew-shared-mac and add it to admin's ~/.zshrc.\r\n  5. Check the result.\r\nUndo: sudo chown -R <your-user> /opt/homebrew\r\n\r\nMake these changes now? [y/N] "]
[17.3654, "o", "y"]
[17.4304, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.4345, "o", "\r\nYou now choose the password for the 'homebrew' account.\r\n  - This account owns every Homebrew file. Keep its password safe.\r\n  - Save it in a password manager now. Do not share it.\r\n  - Do not use a password that you use anywhere else.\r\n  - You rarely need it. You need it if you must change the account later.\r\n\r\n"]
[17.4347, "o", "Password for 'homebrew': "]
[26.5853, "o", "\r\nType it again: "]
[28.5655, "o", "\r\n"]
[28.597, "o", "Creating the hidden account 'homebrew'...\r\n"]
[30.5367, "o", "Created the hidden account 'homebrew'.\r\n"]
[31.6662, "o", "Changed the owner of /opt/homebrew to 'homebrew'.\r\n"]
[31.6737, "o", "Add the brew wrapper to /Users/admin/.zshrc? [y/N] "]
[33.1809, "o", "y"]
[33.2458, "o", "\r\n"]
[33.2806, "o", "Added the wrapper to ~/.zshrc.\r\n"]
[34.3517, "o", "PASS  'homebrew' owns every file in /opt/homebrew\r\n"]
[34.3848, "o", "PASS  brew --version works for admin\r\nPASS  wrapper is in /usr/local/share/homebrew-shared-mac\r\n"]
[34.4562, "o", "PASS  a new Terminal window loads the wrapper\r\n\r\nNext\r\n  1. Close this Terminal window and open a new one.\r\n     Only a new window loads the wrapper. (Or run: source ~/.zshrc)\r\n  2. Test it (this asks for YOUR password): brew update\r\n     If brew says 'not writable' and shows 'sudo chown', do not run that command.\r\n     It means this window does not have the wrapper yet. Open a new window.\r\n"]
[34.4562, "o", "  3. For each other person: log in as that person and run:\r\n       echo 'source /usr/local/share/homebrew-shared-mac/brew-wrapper.zsh' >> ~/.zshrc\r\n\r\nReport for your AI agent: /Users/admin/shared-brew-report-20261124-171000.txt\r\nThe report lists the account names on this Mac. Read it before you share it.\r\n"]
